From 1a4fe86b3cfe3f5ce49a6483c1dd4c412c5a6885 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:44:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Serve the modem's AMMS DRDI copy requests

The modem asks the AP (IPC_RPC_AMMS_DRDI_CONTROL, 0x4014) to copy pieces
of the "md1drdi" entry of the modem partition into the DRDI shared memory
mapped through /dev/ccci_rpc; without them MT6897 modems assert in their
memory manager right after the runtime data. Add an independent responder
written from the request/reply and file traffic observed on a running
Android (no vendor code): a start request answered with the DRDI version,
copy requests carrying up to 15 (source, destination, size) triples, the
last one flagged.

The partition (MTK_CCCI_MODEM_IMAGE) is opened read-only and every copy
is checked against the entry and the 64 KiB window. Offline test with a
synthetic container.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
